      "missing_clauses": [],
      "per_unit_reason": "This is an individually read curriculum introduction naming the tools and content organization used by the modules. It describes the lesson scope and available examples; it does not state an unconditional safety or optimizer guarantee."
    },
    {
      "key": "primer-optimization.html::node-82",
      "source": "SafeLearning/primer-optimization.html",
      "locator": "::node-82",
      "line": 75,
      "tag": "li",
      "classes": [],
      "source_text": "Running example of Sections 6\u20138: minimise $(x-2)^2$ subject to $x\\le1$; solution $x^\\star=1$, optimal value $p^\\star=1$.",
      "text_sha256": "d51ccb42114c81fe6a6c682ebd094de99951d4264771a9a86201c98b0637fedf",
      "source_sha256": "74a2b1cef3b6dbe252f28084a00e848a18befb538d48e08bd76782d1511a6f1b",
      "inventory_kind": "source_unit_needs_claim_review",
      "source_unit_key": "primer-optimization.html::node-82",
      "unit_text_sha256": "d51ccb42114c81fe6a6c682ebd094de99951d4264771a9a86201c98b0637fedf",
      "review_status": "approved_complete_source",
      "material_status": "proved",
      "semantic_kind": "mathematical_statement_or_explicit_domain_convention",
      "hypotheses": [
        "Real variable x with constraint x<=1 and objective exactly(x-2)^2."
      ],
      "lean_declarations": [
        "SafeLearning.CompleteModulesQuadraticDual.actual_primal_unique_global_optimum"
      ],
      "missing_clauses": [],
      "per_unit_reason": "The genuine every-feasible-input lower bound1 and equality iff x=1 prove both solution and optimal value. The actual definition is precisely the printed running objective; the attainer follows by specializing x=1."
    },
    {
      "key": "primer-optimization.html::node-85",
      "source": "SafeLearning/primer-optimization.html",
      "locator": "::node-85",
      "line": 82,
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "source_text": "If differentiation feels rusty, begin with the algebra and calculus refresher. Read Sections 1\u20135 in order before the algorithms. In Section 6, master feasibility, one active constraint and the four KKT checks before the longer constraint-qualification examples. Sections 7\u20138 then connect those tools to solver problems and worst-case decisions.",
      "text_sha256": "8345728f2a72f135aa1c2faf3e0c0a0970b06bca03b89a12236ebc8a8460036b",
      "source_sha256": "74a2b1cef3b6dbe252f28084a00e848a18befb538d48e08bd76782d1511a6f1b",
      "inventory_kind": "surrounding_prose_needs_semantic_classification",
      "source_unit_key": "primer-optimization.html::node-85",
      "unit_text_sha256": "8345728f2a72f135aa1c2faf3e0c0a0970b06bca03b89a12236ebc8a8460036b",
      "review_status": "approved_not_formalizable",
      "material_status": "not_a_formal_claim",
      "semantic_kind": "individual_curriculum_instruction_or_menu",
      "hypotheses": [],
      "lean_declarations": [],
      "missing_clauses": [],
      "per_unit_reason": "Each imperative specifies a reading/learning order. The named four KKT checks are the actual four items in the same page lines934-937; the paragraph makes no theorem about the outcome of studying them."
    },
    {
      "key": "primer-optimization.html::node-87",
      "source": "SafeLearning/primer-optimization.html",
      "locator": "::node-87",
      "line": 83,
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "source_text": "Each of the eight sections has an Easy, Medium and Hard practice sequence: 24 local exercises, in addition to the mixed exercises at the end. Try the question, use the independent hint only when stuck, and write a complete attempt before opening the worked solution. Afterwards close it and reproduce the reasoning.",
      "text_sha256": "3299e74fd2e5bdcd0d6377dfb104c2629f40c3988edb0b358cd8aafa54518665",
      "source_sha256": "74a2b1cef3b6dbe252f28084a00e848a18befb538d48e08bd76782d1511a6f1b",
      "inventory_kind": "surrounding_prose_needs_semantic_classification",
