      "source_text": "Square: $x^2-4x+5=x^2-4x+4+1=(x-2)^2+1$. Since a square is nonnegative, the unique unconstrained minimum is 1 at x=2. If $x\\le1$, the closest permitted x to 2 is x=1, with value 2. The same expression is a different optimisation problem when its domain changes.",
